  "worked_solution": "We write down $E$ and the identity matrix $I$ side-by-side (as shown below) and apply an elementary row operation that transforms the left matrix into the identity matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[E\\,|\\,I\\,] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] &  & {R}_{2}:=-\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2} \\\\  & \u223c[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 & -\\frac{1}{3} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe inverse is obtained on the right-hand side of our big matrix after the transformation. Therefore, \n\n$$\n{E}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{1}{3} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
